create or alter procedure [dbo].[PurgingSP] 
(@TableName nvarchar(400), @AuditTableName nvarchar(400), @RefColumn nvarchar(128), @WhereClause nvarchar(4000), @ChunkSize int = 10000, @MaxDOP int = 1, @BatchDelay nvarchar(12) = '00:00:00')
as
begin
	set nocount on;
	set xact_abort on;
	set deadlock_priority LOW;

	if LEN(@TableName) > 400
	begin
		raiserror ('Parameter @TableName is too long: supplied length is %d characters. Maximum allowed is 400.', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	if LEN(@AuditTableName) > 400
	begin
		raiserror ('Parameter @AuditTableName is too long: supplied length is %d characters. Maximum allowed is 400.', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	if LEN(@RefColumn) > 128
	begin
		raiserror ('Parameter @RefColumn is too long: supplied length is %d characters. Maximum allowed is 128.', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	if LEN(@WhereClause) > 4000
	begin
		raiserror ('Parameter @WhereClause is too long: supplied length is %d characters. Maximum allowed is 4000.', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	if LEN(@BatchDelay) > 12
	begin
		raiserror ('Parameter @BatchDelay is too long: supplied length is %d characters. Maximum allowed is 12 (HH:MM:SS.mmm).', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	if @TableName is null or @AuditTableName is null or @RefColumn is null or @WhereClause is null
	begin
		raiserror ('@TableName, @AuditTableName, @RefColumn, and @WhereClause cannot be NULL.', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	if @ChunkSize <= 0 or @ChunkSize > 50000
	begin
		raiserror ('@ChunkSize must be between 1 and 50000.', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	declare @CompatLevel int;
	declare @RecoveryModel nvarchar(60);

	select @CompatLevel = compatibility_level, @RecoveryModel = recovery_model_desc
	from sys.databases
	where database_id = DB_ID();

	if @CompatLevel < 100
	begin
		raiserror ('Database compatibility level is %d. Must be 100 or higher.', 16, 1, @CompatLevel);

		return;
	end

	declare @CheckpointEnabled bit = case when @RecoveryModel in (N'SIMPLE', N'BULK_LOGGED') then 1 else 0 end;

	print 'Recovery model: ' + @RecoveryModel + case when @CheckpointEnabled = 1 then N' – CHECKPOINT will run every 500 batches.' else N' – Issue LOG BACKUPs to manage log growth.' end;

	declare @DelayEnabled bit = case when @BatchDelay > '00:00:00' then 1 else 0 end;
	declare @Safe bit = [dbo].[fn_IsWhereClauseSafe](@WhereClause);

	if @Safe = 0
	begin
		raiserror ('Unsafe WHERE clause - aborting.', 16, 1);

		return;
	end

	declare @SourceDBName nvarchar(128) = PARSENAME(@TableName, 3);
	declare @SchemaName nvarchar(128) = PARSENAME(@TableName, 2);
	declare @BaseTableName nvarchar(128) = PARSENAME(@TableName, 1);

	if @SourceDBName is null or @SchemaName is null or @BaseTableName is null
	begin
		raiserror ('@TableName must be a fully qualified 3-part name: DatabaseName.SchemaName.TableName. Supplied: ''%s''.', 16, 1, @TableName);

		return;
	end

	declare @FullTableName nvarchar(400) = QUOTENAME(@SourceDBName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@SchemaName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@BaseTableName);
	declare @AuditDBName nvarchar(128) = PARSENAME(@AuditTableName, 3);
	declare @AuditSchemaName nvarchar(128) = ISNULL(PARSENAME(@AuditTableName, 2), N'dbo');
	declare @AuditBaseTable nvarchar(128) = PARSENAME(@AuditTableName, 1);

	if @AuditBaseTable is null
	begin
		set @AuditSchemaName = N'dbo';
		set @AuditBaseTable = @AuditTableName;
	end

	declare @FullAuditName nvarchar(500) = case when @AuditDBName is not null then QUOTENAME(@AuditDBName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@AuditSchemaName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@AuditBaseTable) else QUOTENAME(@AuditSchemaName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@AuditBaseTable) end;
	declare @InstanceName nvarchar(128) = ISNULL(@@SERVERNAME, CAST(SERVERPROPERTY('ServerName') as nvarchar(128)));
	declare @SysColsDB nvarchar(200) = case when @AuditDBName is not null then QUOTENAME(@AuditDBName) + N'.sys.columns' else N'sys.columns' end;
	declare @IsSelfPurge bit = 0;
	declare @FullAuditName3Part nvarchar(500) = case when @AuditDBName is not null then QUOTENAME(@AuditDBName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@AuditSchemaName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@AuditBaseTable) else QUOTENAME(@SourceDBName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@AuditSchemaName) + N'.' + QUOTENAME(@AuditBaseTable) end;

	if UPPER(@FullTableName) = UPPER(@FullAuditName3Part)
	begin
		set @IsSelfPurge = 1;

		print 'Self-purge mode: @TableName and @AuditTableName resolve to the same table (' + @FullTableName + N'). All audit logging suppressed for this run.';
	end

	declare @AuditErrMsg nvarchar(4000);
	declare @OrphanErrMsg nvarchar(4000);
	declare @GuardErrMsg nvarchar(4000);
	declare @InitErrMsg nvarchar(4000);
	declare @InitFailTime datetime2(3);
	declare @AuditWriteErr nvarchar(4000);
	declare @LoopErrMsg nvarchar(4000);
	declare @LoopErrLine int;
	declare @FinalRangeMessage nvarchar(500);

	if @IsSelfPurge = 0
	begin
		begin try
			declare @TableExists int;
			declare @CheckSQL nvarchar(500) = N'SELECT @exists = CASE WHEN OBJECT_ID(@fullname, ''U'') IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END';

			exec sp_executesql @CheckSQL, N'@fullname NVARCHAR(500), @exists INT OUTPUT', @fullname = @FullAuditName, @exists = @TableExists output;

			if @TableExists = 0
			begin
				declare @CreateSQL nvarchar(MAX) = N'CREATE TABLE ' + @FullAuditName + N'
(
    AuditID           INT IDENTITY(1,1) NOT NULL,
    InstanceName      NVARCHAR(128)     NOT NULL,
    DBName            NVARCHAR(128)     NOT NULL,
    SessionID         INT               NULL,
    TableName         NVARCHAR(400)     NOT NULL,
    BatchSize         INT               NOT NULL,
    TotalRowsInRange  INT               NOT NULL,
    RowsDeleted       INT               NOT NULL,
    RowsLeftToDelete  INT               NOT NULL,
    BatchStartTime    DATETIME2(3)      NOT NULL,
    BatchEndTime      DATETIME2(3)      NOT NULL,
    RangeDeletion     NVARCHAR(500)     NOT NULL,
    [Status]          NVARCHAR(50)      NOT NULL,
    ErrorMessage      NVARCHAR(4000)    NULL
    CONSTRAINT PK_PurgeAuditLog PRIMARY KEY CLUSTERED (AuditID)
);
CREATE NONCLUSTERED INDEX IX_PurgeAudit_Table_Status
    ON ' + @FullAuditName + 
					N'
    (TableName, [Status], BatchEndTime DESC)
    INCLUDE (SessionID, RowsLeftToDelete, TotalRowsInRange, RowsDeleted);';

				exec sp_executesql @CreateSQL;

				print 'Audit table created: ' + @FullAuditName;
			end
			else
			begin
				declare @SchemaUpgradeSQL nvarchar(MAX) = N'IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ' + @SysColsDB + N' WHERE object_id = OBJECT_ID(''' + @FullAuditName + N''') AND name = ''SessionID'')
                        ALTER TABLE ' + @FullAuditName + N' ADD SessionID INT NULL;' + N'IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ' + @SysColsDB + N' WHERE object_id = OBJECT_ID(''' + @FullAuditName + N''') AND name = ''DBName'')
                        ALTER TABLE ' + @FullAuditName + N' ADD DBName NVARCHAR(128) NULL;' + N'IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ' + @SysColsDB + N' WHERE object_id = OBJECT_ID(''' + @FullAuditName + N''') AND name = ''InstanceName'')
                        ALTER TABLE ' + @FullAuditName + N' ADD InstanceName NVARCHAR(128) NULL;';

				exec sp_executesql @SchemaUpgradeSQL;
			end
		end try

		begin catch
			set @AuditErrMsg = ERROR_MESSAGE();

			raiserror ('Failed to ensure audit table exists: %s', 16, 1, @AuditErrMsg);

			return;
		end catch
	end

	declare @BatchNumber int = 0;
	declare @RowsDeleted int = 0;
	declare @TotalDeleted int = 0;
	declare @RowsLeftToDelete int = 0;
	declare @TotalRowsInRange int = 0;
	declare @BatchStartTime datetime2(3);
	declare @BatchEndTime datetime2(3);
	declare @RangeMessage nvarchar(500);
	declare @BatchRangeMessage nvarchar(500);
	declare @MinRefValue nvarchar(50);
	declare @MaxRefValue nvarchar(50);
	declare @BatchMinRefValue nvarchar(50);
	declare @BatchMaxRefValue nvarchar(50);
	declare @SQL nvarchar(MAX);
	declare @CurrentBatchAuditID int;
	declare @CurrentSessionID int = @@SPID;
	declare @ScratchAuditID int;
	declare @BatchFinalStatus nvarchar(50);
	declare @BatchErrMsg nvarchar(4000);
	declare @BatchRangeScalarTemplate nvarchar(MAX) = N'SELECT
            @BatchMinOut = MIN(src.' + QUOTENAME(@RefColumn) + N'),
            @BatchMaxOut = MAX(src.' + QUOTENAME(@RefColumn) + N')
         FROM (
             SELECT TOP (@ChunkSizeParam) ' + QUOTENAME(@RefColumn) + N'
             FROM ' + @FullTableName + N'
             WHERE ' + @WhereClause + N'
             ORDER BY (SELECT NULL)
         ) AS src;';
	declare @BatchRangeParamDef nvarchar(200) = N'@ChunkSizeParam INT, @BatchMinOut NVARCHAR(50) OUTPUT, @BatchMaxOut NVARCHAR(50) OUTPUT';
	-- DELETE template.
	declare @DeleteTemplate nvarchar(MAX) = N'DELETE TOP (@ChunkSizeParam)
          FROM ' + @FullTableName + N'
          WHERE ' + @WhereClause + N'
          OPTION (MAXDOP ' + CAST(@MaxDOP as nvarchar(2)) + N');';
	declare @AuditInsertTemplate nvarchar(MAX) = N'INSERT INTO ' + @FullAuditName + N'
            (DBName, InstanceName, SessionID, TableName, BatchSize,
             TotalRowsInRange, RowsDeleted, RowsLeftToDelete,
             BatchStartTime, BatchEndTime, RangeDeletion, [Status], ErrorMessage)
          VALUES
            (@DBNameParam, @InstanceNameParam, @SessionIDParam,
             @TableNameParam, @ChunkSizeParam, @TotalRowsInRangeParam, @RowsDeletedParam,
             @RowsLeftToDeleteParam, @BatchStartTimeParam, @BatchEndTimeParam,
             @RangeMessageParam, @StatusParam, @ErrMsgParam);
          SELECT @NewAuditIDParam = SCOPE_IDENTITY();';
	declare @AuditInsertParamDef nvarchar(MAX) = N'@DBNameParam          NVARCHAR(128),
          @InstanceNameParam    NVARCHAR(128),
          @SessionIDParam       INT,
          @TableNameParam       NVARCHAR(400),
          @ChunkSizeParam       INT,
          @TotalRowsInRangeParam INT,
          @RowsDeletedParam     INT,
          @RowsLeftToDeleteParam INT,
          @BatchStartTimeParam  DATETIME2(3),
          @BatchEndTimeParam    DATETIME2(3),
          @RangeMessageParam    NVARCHAR(500),
          @StatusParam          NVARCHAR(50),
          @ErrMsgParam          NVARCHAR(4000),
          @NewAuditIDParam      INT OUTPUT';
	declare @AuditUpdateTemplate nvarchar(MAX) = N'UPDATE ' + @FullAuditName + N'
          SET [Status]         = @StatusParam,
              BatchEndTime     = @BatchEndTimeParam,
              RowsDeleted      = @RowsDeletedParam,
              RowsLeftToDelete = @RowsLeftToDeleteParam,
              TotalRowsInRange = @TotalRowsInRangeParam,
              ErrorMessage     = @ErrMsgParam,
              RangeDeletion    = @RangeMessageParam
          WHERE AuditID = @AuditIDParam;';
	declare @AuditUpdateParamDef nvarchar(MAX) = N'@AuditIDParam         INT,
          @StatusParam          NVARCHAR(50),
          @BatchEndTimeParam    DATETIME2(3),
          @RowsDeletedParam     INT,
          @RowsLeftToDeleteParam INT,
          @TotalRowsInRangeParam INT,
          @ErrMsgParam          NVARCHAR(4000),
          @RangeMessageParam    NVARCHAR(500)';

	set @SQL = N'SELECT
            @MinRef = COALESCE(CAST(MIN(' + QUOTENAME(@RefColumn) + N') AS NVARCHAR(50)), N''NoRecordsFound''),
            @MaxRef = COALESCE(CAST(MAX(' + QUOTENAME(@RefColumn) + N') AS NVARCHAR(50)), N''NoRecordsFound'')
          FROM ' + @FullTableName + N'
          WHERE ' + @WhereClause + N';';

	exec sp_executesql @SQL, N'@MinRef NVARCHAR(50) OUTPUT, @MaxRef NVARCHAR(50) OUTPUT', @MinRef = @MinRefValue output, @MaxRef = @MaxRefValue output;

	set @RangeMessage = N'FullRange: ' + ISNULL(@MinRefValue, N'N/A') + N' to ' + ISNULL(@MaxRefValue, N'N/A');

	if @IsSelfPurge = 0
	begin
		begin try
			declare @OrphanAuditID int;
			declare @OrphanSessionID int;

			set @SQL = N'SELECT TOP 1
                    @OrphanAuditIDOut  = AuditID,
                    @OrphanSessionIDOut = SessionID
                  FROM ' + @FullAuditName + N'
                  WHERE TableName  = @TableNameParam
                    AND [Status]   = ''RUNNING''
                  ORDER BY AuditID DESC;';

			exec sp_executesql @SQL, N'@TableNameParam    NVARCHAR(400),
                  @OrphanAuditIDOut  INT OUTPUT,
                  @OrphanSessionIDOut INT OUTPUT', @TableNameParam = @TableName, @OrphanAuditIDOut = @OrphanAuditID output, @OrphanSessionIDOut = @OrphanSessionID output;

			if @OrphanAuditID is not null
			begin
				declare @SessionTrulyAlive int = 0;

				select @SessionTrulyAlive = COUNT(1)
				from sys.dm_exec_sessions s
				join sys.dm_exec_requests r on r.session_id = s.session_id
				where s.session_id = @OrphanSessionID and r.status = 'running';

				if @SessionTrulyAlive = 0
				begin
					set @BatchEndTime = SYSDATETIME();

					exec sp_executesql @AuditUpdateTemplate, @AuditUpdateParamDef, @AuditIDParam = @OrphanAuditID, @StatusParam = N'KILLED', @BatchEndTimeParam = @BatchEndTime, @RowsDeletedParam = 0, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = 0, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = 0, @ErrMsgParam = N'Session was killed/stopped/disconnected. Purge resuming.', @RangeMessageParam = @RangeMessage;
				end
				else
				begin
					print 'RUNNING row found with active executing request. Concurrent guard will block.';
				end
			end
		end try

		begin catch
			set @OrphanErrMsg = ERROR_MESSAGE();

			raiserror ('Orphan handler failed: %s', 16, 1, @OrphanErrMsg);

			return;
		end catch
	end

	if @IsSelfPurge = 0
	begin
		begin try
			declare @LiveRunning int = 0;

			set @SQL = N'SELECT @LiveRunningOut = COUNT(1)
                  FROM ' + @FullAuditName + N' a
                  JOIN sys.dm_exec_requests r ON r.session_id = a.SessionID
                  WHERE a.TableName = @TableNameParam
                    AND a.[Status]  = ''RUNNING'';';

			exec sp_executesql @SQL, N'@TableNameParam NVARCHAR(400), @LiveRunningOut INT OUTPUT', @TableNameParam = @TableName, @LiveRunningOut = @LiveRunning output;

			if @LiveRunning > 0
			begin
				raiserror ('Table ''%s'' is already being purged by an actively executing session.', 16, 1, @TableName);

				return;
			end
		end try

		begin catch
			set @GuardErrMsg = ERROR_MESSAGE();

			raiserror ('Concurrent run guard failed: %s', 16, 1, @GuardErrMsg);

			return;
		end catch
	end

	begin try
		set @BatchStartTime = SYSDATETIME();
		set @BatchEndTime = @BatchStartTime;
		set @SQL = N'SELECT @RowsLeftOut = CAST(COUNT_BIG(1) AS INT)
              FROM ' + @FullTableName + N'
              WHERE ' + @WhereClause + N';';

		exec sp_executesql @SQL, N'@RowsLeftOut INT OUTPUT', @RowsLeftOut = @RowsLeftToDelete output;

		set @TotalRowsInRange = @RowsLeftToDelete;

		if @RowsLeftToDelete = 0
		begin
			if @IsSelfPurge = 0
			begin
				exec sp_executesql @AuditInsertTemplate, @AuditInsertParamDef, @DBNameParam = @SourceDBName, @InstanceNameParam = @InstanceName, @SessionIDParam = @CurrentSessionID, @TableNameParam = @TableName, @ChunkSizeParam = @ChunkSize, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = 0, @RowsDeletedParam = 0, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = 0, @BatchStartTimeParam = @BatchStartTime, @BatchEndTimeParam = @BatchEndTime, @RangeMessageParam = @RangeMessage, @StatusParam = N'NO_RECORDS_FOUND', @ErrMsgParam = null, @NewAuditIDParam = @ScratchAuditID output;
			end

			print 'No rows match the WHERE clause. Nothing to purge.';

			return;
		end

		if @IsSelfPurge = 0
		begin
			exec sp_executesql @AuditInsertTemplate, @AuditInsertParamDef, @DBNameParam = @SourceDBName, @InstanceNameParam = @InstanceName, @SessionIDParam = @CurrentSessionID, @TableNameParam = @TableName, @ChunkSizeParam = @ChunkSize, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = @TotalRowsInRange, @RowsDeletedParam = 0, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = @RowsLeftToDelete, @BatchStartTimeParam = @BatchStartTime, @BatchEndTimeParam = @BatchEndTime, @RangeMessageParam = @RangeMessage, @StatusParam = N'STARTED', @ErrMsgParam = @WhereClause, @NewAuditIDParam = @ScratchAuditID output;
		end
	end try

	begin catch
		set @InitErrMsg = ERROR_MESSAGE();
		set @InitFailTime = SYSDATETIME();

		if @IsSelfPurge = 0
		begin
			begin try
				exec sp_executesql @AuditInsertTemplate, @AuditInsertParamDef, @DBNameParam = @SourceDBName, @InstanceNameParam = @InstanceName, @SessionIDParam = @CurrentSessionID, @TableNameParam = @TableName, @ChunkSizeParam = @ChunkSize, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = @TotalRowsInRange, @RowsDeletedParam = 0, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = @RowsLeftToDelete, @BatchStartTimeParam = @BatchStartTime, @BatchEndTimeParam = @InitFailTime, @RangeMessageParam = @RangeMessage, @StatusParam = N'FAILED', @ErrMsgParam = @InitErrMsg, @NewAuditIDParam = @ScratchAuditID output;
			end try

			begin catch
				set @AuditWriteErr = ERROR_MESSAGE();

				raiserror ('Init FAILED audit write also failed: %s | Original error: %s', 16, 1, @AuditWriteErr, @InitErrMsg);

				return;
			end catch
		end

		raiserror ('Initial setup failed: %s', 16, 1, @InitErrMsg);

		return;
	end catch

	begin try
		set @BatchNumber = 1;

		while @RowsLeftToDelete > 0
		begin
			set @BatchNumber += 1;
			set @BatchStartTime = SYSDATETIME();

			exec sp_executesql @BatchRangeScalarTemplate, @BatchRangeParamDef, @ChunkSizeParam = @ChunkSize, @BatchMinOut = @BatchMinRefValue output, @BatchMaxOut = @BatchMaxRefValue output;

			set @BatchRangeMessage = N'BatchRange: ' + ISNULL(@BatchMinRefValue, N'N/A') + N' to ' + ISNULL(@BatchMaxRefValue, N'N/A');
			set @CurrentBatchAuditID = null;

			if @IsSelfPurge = 0
			begin
				begin try
					exec sp_executesql @AuditInsertTemplate, @AuditInsertParamDef, @DBNameParam = @SourceDBName, @InstanceNameParam = @InstanceName, @SessionIDParam = @CurrentSessionID, @TableNameParam = @TableName, @ChunkSizeParam = @ChunkSize, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = @TotalRowsInRange, @RowsDeletedParam = 0, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = @RowsLeftToDelete, @BatchStartTimeParam = @BatchStartTime, @BatchEndTimeParam = @BatchStartTime, @RangeMessageParam = @BatchRangeMessage, @StatusParam = N'RUNNING', @ErrMsgParam = null, @NewAuditIDParam = @CurrentBatchAuditID output;
				end try

				begin catch
					set @BatchErrMsg = ERROR_MESSAGE();
					set @BatchEndTime = SYSDATETIME();

					exec sp_executesql @AuditInsertTemplate, @AuditInsertParamDef, @DBNameParam = @SourceDBName, @InstanceNameParam = @InstanceName, @SessionIDParam = @CurrentSessionID, @TableNameParam = @TableName, @ChunkSizeParam = @ChunkSize, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = @TotalRowsInRange, @RowsDeletedParam = @RowsDeleted, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = @RowsLeftToDelete, @BatchStartTimeParam = @BatchStartTime, @BatchEndTimeParam = @BatchEndTime, @RangeMessageParam = @BatchRangeMessage, @StatusParam = N'FAILED', @ErrMsgParam = @BatchErrMsg, @NewAuditIDParam = @ScratchAuditID output;

					raiserror ('Audit RUNNING INSERT failed at batch %d: %s', 16, 1, @BatchNumber, @BatchErrMsg);

					return;
				end catch
			end

			exec sp_executesql @DeleteTemplate, N'@ChunkSizeParam INT', @ChunkSizeParam = @ChunkSize;

			set @RowsDeleted = @@ROWCOUNT;
			set @TotalDeleted += @RowsDeleted;
			set @BatchEndTime = SYSDATETIME();
			set @RowsLeftToDelete -= @RowsDeleted;

			if @RowsLeftToDelete < 0
				set @RowsLeftToDelete = 0;
			set @BatchFinalStatus = case when @RowsLeftToDelete = 0 then N'SUCCESS' else N'COMPLETED' end;

			if @IsSelfPurge = 0
			begin
				set @BatchErrMsg = case when @BatchFinalStatus = N'SUCCESS' then @WhereClause else null end;

				exec sp_executesql @AuditUpdateTemplate, @AuditUpdateParamDef, @AuditIDParam = @CurrentBatchAuditID, @StatusParam = @BatchFinalStatus, @BatchEndTimeParam = @BatchEndTime, @RowsDeletedParam = @RowsDeleted, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = @RowsLeftToDelete, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = @TotalRowsInRange, @ErrMsgParam = @BatchErrMsg, @RangeMessageParam = @BatchRangeMessage;
			end

			if @CheckpointEnabled = 1 and @BatchNumber % 500 = 0
				checkpoint;

			if @DelayEnabled = 1
				waitfor delay @BatchDelay;
		end

		print 'Purge completed. Total rows deleted: ' + CAST(@TotalDeleted as nvarchar(20)) + ' Batches: ' + CAST((@BatchNumber - 1) as nvarchar(20));
	end try

	begin catch
		set @LoopErrMsg = ERROR_MESSAGE();
		set @LoopErrLine = ERROR_LINE();
		set @BatchEndTime = SYSDATETIME();
		set @FinalRangeMessage = ISNULL(@BatchRangeMessage, @RangeMessage);

		if @@TRANCOUNT > 0
			rollback transaction;

		if @IsSelfPurge = 0 and @CurrentBatchAuditID is not null
		begin
			exec sp_executesql @AuditUpdateTemplate, @AuditUpdateParamDef, @AuditIDParam = @CurrentBatchAuditID, @StatusParam = N'FAILED', @BatchEndTimeParam = @BatchEndTime, @RowsDeletedParam = @RowsDeleted, @RowsLeftToDeleteParam = @RowsLeftToDelete, @TotalRowsInRangeParam = @TotalRowsInRange, @ErrMsgParam = @LoopErrMsg,
				@RangeMessageParam = @FinalRangeMessage;
		end

		raiserror ('PurgingSP failed at line %d – %s – Range: %s', 16, 1, @LoopErrLine, @LoopErrMsg, @FinalRangeMessage);
	end catch
end;
go

